{
  "comment": "The one table of cases that the GitHub App (tests/review-runner.test.ts and tests/review-outcome.test.ts) and the Actions workflow (tests/unit/test_review_not_run_exit.py and test_review_publish_incomplete.py, which run the inline script of .github/workflows/trelix-review.yml under node) are both tested against. It fixes what the Check says for each way `trelix review` can end. exit_code is what the workflow step records (a string; null = it recorded nothing). severities is the severity of each finding `trelix review --json` printed, in order. stdout_text, when present, is what `trelix review --json` printed instead (text that is not a JSON array of objects, so the findings cannot be read; severities is then empty): the Check must say so and never read it as \"found 0 issue(s)\" or as a review that is clean, and its conclusion is neutral whatever the exit code. outcome applies to exit 4 only: valid = the record in valid_outcome, missing = no file, corrupt = a file that is not JSON. applies_to lists the sides the row is run on; omitted means both. Keep the titles and conclusions literal. invalid_outcomes are records (raw text, so that NaN and cut-off documents can be written) that both sides must read as unknown: the App's parseOutcomeRecord and the workflow's readOutcome.",
